id: design.timeout-classification
kind: design
title: timeout classification (retryable vs terminal)
aliases: timeout classification, retryable timeout, timeout taxonomy
tags: design, timeouts, retries, resilience
questions:
  - is a timeout always worth retrying?
  - how do you tell a transient timeout from a dead server?
invariant: Not every timeout is worth retrying; a timeout that fired late after a long wait is usually not the same failure as one at the boundary.
answer_30s: Classify timeouts as boundary (retry; the remote was probably busy) vs late (do not retry; the remote may already be acting on the request); pair that classification with a circuit breaker and an idempotent call so retry is safe.
when_to_use:
  - deciding whether to retry after a timeout
  - tuning a circuit breaker's response to timeouts
related:
  - design.retry-backoff
  - design.circuit-breaker
  - design.retry-idempotency
sources:
  - https://sre.google/sre-book/
